{
  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "5D8B1ED2-B3E9-4CFC-8459-A84A85F39914",
      "rect": [
        [
          -40,
          -480
        ],
        [
          720,
          400
        ]
      ],
      "note": "# Supershape Morph\n\n**Super Shape Geometry** is Gielis' superformula applied twice - once for\nthe horizontal profile, once for the vertical - and its two symmetry\ncounts **M1** and **M2** decide how many lobes each profile has. Here a\nMath Expression drifts both, plus the first profile's sharpness **N11**,\nso the body melts between stars, flowers, cushions and shells.\n\nNon-integer M is where the interesting tears happen: the profile no\nlonger closes on itself and seams open briefly as it passes between\nwhole lobe counts. **rate** sets how fast it morphs; the drifts run at\nunrelated speeds so the form never quite repeats."
    },
    {
      "id": "041D4DC1-74E2-4D26-B563-CD066D9D6E60",
      "rect": [
        [
          760,
          -480
        ],
        [
          520,
          280
        ]
      ],
      "note": "## Try\n\nDisconnect *m1* and drag **M1** by hand while M2 keeps moving. Push the\n**N2x** / **N3x** exponents below 1 for spiky, above 2 for puffy. A warm key\nand a cool fill light pick out the lobes from opposite sides."
    }
  ],
  "id": "4194E7A8-0EDB-450D-BE1B-E3F81742A7A4",
  "version": {
    "beta": {}
  },
